---
title: Track your course status
description: Where you see your proposals, how to pick a draft back up, and where your course gets reviewed.
sidebar:
  order: 6
---

**My courses** ([/become-a-teacher/courses](https://ismos.xyz/become-a-teacher/courses/)) lists the status of every course you've proposed. If you haven't proposed any yet you'll see *"You don't have any courses yet"* and a **Propose a course** button.

## Drafts

A course you started and didn't submit shows up as a **draft**, with a link to continue right where you left off. Nothing has to be redone: the form saves itself.

## Submitted proposals

Once submitted, the course carries a link to its **Pull Request** on GitHub. That Pull Request is where the review actually happens: comments, change requests and approval. It's worth turning on GitHub notifications so you hear about replies.

## Back to the campus

From your instructor space, **Go to Moodle** takes you to the campus. They're separate accounts: teaching doesn't automatically give you a student account, or the other way round.
